.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt FILEES-ADMIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-admin
.Nd FileES administrative tickets, revocation and erasure closure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket create Ar mailbox
.Op Fl -ttl Ar duration
.Op Fl -join-realm-alias Ar alias
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket resend Fl -ticket-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket revoke Fl -ticket-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket list
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm operation inspect Fl -operation-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm client revoke Fl -client-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm client revoke-realm Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm repo transfer-owner Fl -repo-id Ar uuid Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm erasure complete Fl -operation-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -partially-retained
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the operator command for onboarding tickets and a small set of
fail-closed administrative actions.
It writes structured JSON to standard output and diagnostics to standard
error.
It must run with effective user
.Sy _filees-state .
Creating a ticket as root produces a root-owned mode 0600 file that the
set-id onboarding entry intentionally cannot read.
.Pp
.Cm version
is answered before the configuration is opened, so a stale binary can be
identified even when
.Pa server.json
is suspect.
.Pp
Repository create, grants, public shares and realm removal are desktop
control-plane operations, not extra
.Nm
verbs.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ticket create
Issue a one-time invitation to
.Ar mailbox
and send it immediately.
The mailbox must come before any flag.
Without
.Fl -join-realm-alias
the ticket authorises a new realm.
With the flag the server resolves the immutable alias now and stores the
approved realm ID; the client never submits that ID.
The invitation capability is not printed.
.It Cm ticket resend
Replace a failed delivery capability without changing recipient or TTL.
.It Cm ticket revoke
Delete an unused ticket.
A claimed ticket has already been replaced by an operation bundle.
.It Cm ticket list
List remaining tickets.
Names are
.Fn sha256 mailbox
so the file name does not reveal the address.
.It Cm operation inspect
Show one onboarding operation.
.It Cm client revoke
Write a durable
.Cm revoking
record, drop generated SSH/SVN access, then commit the revoked client.
An identical retry is idempotent; a different reason is rejected.
.It Cm client revoke-realm
Revoke every installation of a realm with the same sequence.
.It Cm repo transfer-owner
Change
.Ic owner_realm_id
and regenerate data-authz.
Existing grants issued by the previous owner are not touched.
.It Cm erasure complete
Close a data-erasure request after the operator has verified backup
retention.
.Fl -partially-retained
records that policy still requires some copies.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
uses
.Xr sysexits 3
values:
.Bl -tag -width 4n -compact
.It 0
success
.It 64
bad arguments
.It 65
input data error
.It 69
resource unavailable
.It 70
internal error
.It 75
temporary failure
.It 78
configuration error
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a new-realm invitation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin ticket create user@example.com
.Ed
.Pp
Authorise another desktop in an existing realm:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin ticket create user@example.com \e
    --join-realm-alias acme --ttl 24h
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees 7 ,
.Xr filees.conf 5 ,
.Xr filees-operation 8 ,
.Xr filees-mail 8
